# Reproduction for bd inc-hy9u. Two wizard commands, in sequence, as
# acceptance criterion 1 asks: "All Monster Aggravate" then "All Monsters
# Retarget". The aggravate entry crashed the session. src/Debug.cpp:1005
# (case 29) passed myHandle -- an object handle -- as the sixth argument of
# GainPermStati, which is a resource id (rID eID, inc/Map.h). Thing::
# GainPermStati then runs ASSERT(theGame->Get(eID)) (src/Status.cpp:197) on a
# number that names no resource, Game::Get logs "resource id 129 names module
# slot -1, out of range", and the process segfaults. Retarget (case 26) had no
# defect; it is exercised here only so the run covers both commands.
#
# Read by tools/check_wizard_aggravate.sh. The fix passes 0 there, the same
# shape as src/Main.cpp:937 and src/Player.cpp:222; after it the aggravate
# completes and the next turn may be dumped. On the unfixed build the
# after-turn dump is never written and errors.log carries the ASSERT line.
#
# Navigation follows tools/keys/breath-dice-dragon.keys lines 1-40: chargen
# ends in play mode, so the first key is a game command, not a prompt
# dismissal. Enter wizard mode with 'w' (the first entry asks for
# confirmation: 'y'), turn the Wizard Mode Switches on ('w', the menu,
# SPACE, ESC), then summon and aggravate.
@include chargen.keys

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
SPACE
ESC

# One monster, summoned beside the player. Kobolds has a single kind whose
# prompt list is short, so the wording below is a named pick, not a count.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Kobolds"
@choose "kobold"
LEFT ENTER              # adjacent west of the player
@dump:summoned

# This is the crashing entry on the unfixed build.
w
@choose "All Monster Aggravate"
@dump:after-aggravate

# The second wizard command of criterion 1: "All Monsters Retarget" (case 26).
# It had no defect; run here only so the sequence covers both commands.
w
@choose "All Monsters Retarget"
@dump:after-retarget

# One turn, so the aggravate's effect is allowed to settle; the dump after it
# is the check's evidence that the session survived.
.
@dump:after-turn
@quit
